# inc-glnx case 30: cast Command on a summoned rat so its hText str is assigned.
# inc-d9iot: the character is the base save (restored, not generated).
# Controls: no monster acts (Genocide Everything, then Freeze Monsters on the
# one rat summoned as target), the cast cannot fail, and the check sets
# INCURSION_FORCE_SAVE_ROLL=20 so the rat's Will save always resists. The
# target is the rat, not the caster: Magic.cpp:1423 gives a self-target no save.
@expect "Initial Choices"
@choose "Restore a Saved Game"
@expect "Choose a character:"
a
@until "Things in View" ESC
w y
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Genocide Everything"
SPACE*40
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Wizard Mode Switches"
DOWN*5 SPACE            # Row 6: Ignore Spell Failure ON.
DOWN*5 SPACE            # Row 11: Freeze Monsters ON.
ESC
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Change terrain type"   # the square east of the player becomes plain
RIGHT ENTER                     #   floor, whatever the seed's map put there
e                               # [e] Floor ("Floor" and "Floor;2" show the same
                                #   name, so @choose cannot pick one)
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Monster Summoning"
@choose "Animals"
@choose "giant rat"
RIGHT ENTER
@while "more --" SPACE
@until "Wizard Mode Options:" w
@choose "Learn Any Spell"
"Command" ENTER
m
@choose "Command"
l
RIGHT ENTER
h
@dump:command-cast
@quit
